src/reclaim/ai/models/*.onnx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Bundled MiniLM tokenizer config is JSON (text-looking) but its bytes are integrity-checked
# against a pinned SHA256 (reclaim.ai.text_embeddings._TOKENIZER_SHA256) -- git's default
# text-file CRLF normalization (core.autocrlf=true, this repo's committed content is LF-only)
# silently corrupts it on checkout for any contributor/CI runner with that Windows-default git
# setting, breaking every near-dup-document AI code path with a confusing
# `AIModelMissingError: ... failed integrity verification` far from the real cause. Discovered
# via evals/test_e2e_scale.py (Wave 1 P0-C) failing exactly this way in a fresh worktree
# checkout while the primary checkout (a pre-existing, not-freshly-recloned working copy) stayed
# unaffected -- `-text` here is the same fix `*.onnx` already has, extended to this one other
# integrity-checked bundled model file.
src/reclaim/ai/models/*.json -text
# The planner eval's cases are written by evals/fixtures/assistant_mcp/build_planner_cases.py
# with LF, and evals/test_assistant_planner_eval.py re-runs it to prove they are current: kept LF
# on checkout too, so that check (and every run of it) leaves the working tree unchanged.
evals/fixtures/assistant_mcp/*.json text eol=lf
